                        ],
                        "form": "adverted"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "0ce4409c-7ad8-47f3-84c7-82c5a6aca34d",
                        "entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "tags": [
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "adverted"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "059c8abd-2fd7-3b21-a064-ae18cae712d6",
                        "entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To take notice, to pay attention (to)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ef25ad58-c7fd-4ea7-b09e-5d952d6a25db",
                                "sense_id": "059c8abd-2fd7-3b21-a064-ae18cae712d6",
                                "text": "At a time when creation seems to be endangered in so many ways through human activity, we should consciously advert to this dimension of Sunday, too."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c39b2a5b-5762-3b1d-af6c-3b51b5446d5a",
                        "entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To turn attention to, to take notice of (something)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ab770b82-7a59-3a91-9f1c-f06c8bbc057a",
                        "entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To turn attention to, to take notice of (something).",
                            "To turn the attention (of something or someone) (to or toward) some object)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "27efe7d4-c48a-4f68-9fd8-b80b13c4e2c9",
                                "sense_id": "ab770b82-7a59-3a91-9f1c-f06c8bbc057a",
                                "text": "To meditate, one must advert the mind toward the breath"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efa17b13-4fba-3e8a-a8cb-74e8e68d1688",
                        "entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To call attention, refer (to)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "be29e264-c564-423b-84ee-ec9f1f7b8f98",
                                "sense_id": "efa17b13-4fba-3e8a-a8cb-74e8e68d1688",
                                "text": "‘I have before suggested that a genuine blackguard is never without a pocket-handkerchief. But it is not to this fact that I now especially advert.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e0b7182-ba7c-428a-8b14-a6558f614b38",
                                "sense_id": "efa17b13-4fba-3e8a-a8cb-74e8e68d1688",
                                "text": "As soon as Miss Fairlie had left the room he spared us all embarrassment on the subject of the anonymous letter, by adverting to it of his own accord."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25f1d465-786d-4815-b458-5baf1d7e69db",
                                "sense_id": "efa17b13-4fba-3e8a-a8cb-74e8e68d1688",
                                "text": "In this context, it is worth remark that Sir Brian should have paid particular attention to the importance of a reserve of power in locomotives. He adverted to this in a discussion of punctuality, making first the highly debatable assertion that \"a very high proportion\" of steam locomotives today were being worked to the limit of their capacity, with little or no reserve in hand, [...]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2216852a-cd0b-4cf1-ae78-e8928fa849a7",
                        "source_entry_id": "d91c57d1-a2e5-3fb5-8bef-6206d9fb1bde",
                        "source_sense_description": "To turn attention",
                        "target_lang_word": "verwijzen",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
